      <div type="clause" n="42.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 42.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="74" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he mægnes hæbbe, þæt he his gefán beride ⁊ inne besitte, gehealde hine VII niht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.18"/> inne ⁊ hine ón ne feohte, gif he inne geðolian wille; ⁊ þonne ymb VII<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.19"/> niht, gif he wille on hand gan ⁊ wæpenu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.20"/> sellan, gehealde hine XXX nihta gesundne ⁊ hine his mægum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.13"/> gebodie ⁊ his friondum.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.21"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42.1" corresp="#wit-ot-frags"><pb n="74" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf he mæ.. hæbbe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he his ... ⁊ inne besitte, gehe..de hine ....ine on ne feohte, gif he inne geþ ...; .. e ymb VII niht, gif he wille on ... an, gehealde hine XXX n... magum gebodie ⁊ hi...</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="74" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he mægnes hæbbe, ðæt he his gefán beríde ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.5"/> hine inne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.7"/> besitte, gehealde hine seofan niht inne ⁊ him on ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.14"/> feohte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.15"/>, gif he inne geðolian<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.16"/> wille; ⁊ þonne ymb<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.17"/> seofan niht, gif he wille on<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.18-2"/> hond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.5"/> gan ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.5"/> (his<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.7"/>) wæpnu syllan, gehealde hine XXX nihta gesundne ⁊ hine his freondum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.19-2"/> ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.20-2"/> his magum bebeode.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.21-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="42.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="75" ed="#liebermann"/>Si uim habeat, ut inimicum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.13-2"/> (hostem) suum circumueniat et obsideat, custodiat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.14-2"/> eum septem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.15-2"/> noctibus intus nec assalliat eum, si ille<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.16-2"/> uelit immorari.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.oe.17-2"/> Si uelit in manus ire et arma sua reddere, custodiat eum XXX noctibus illesum et parentibus suis eum offerat et amicis.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="82" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif he mægnes hæbbe, þæt he his gefán beride ⁊ inne<ptr type="editorNote" n="17" target="#Af_42-1.attnote.fn.17"/> besitte, gehealde hine VII niht inne ⁊ hine<ptr type="editorNote" n="18" target="#Af_42-1.attnote.fn.18"/> ón ne feohte, gif he inne geðolian wille; ⁊ þonne ymb VII niht, gif he wille on<ptr type="editorNote" n="19" target="#Af_42-1.attnote.fn.19"/> hand gan ⁊ [his]<ptr type="editorNote" n="20" target="#Af_42-1.attnote.fn.20"/> wæpenu sellan, gehealde hine XXX nihta gesundne ⁊ hine his mægum gebodie<ptr type="editorNote" n="21" target="#Af_42-1.attnote.fn.21"/> ⁊ his friondum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="44.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="342" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif he mægnes hæbbe, þæt he his gefán beride ⁊ inne besitte, gehealde hine VII niht inne ⁊ hine ón ne feohte, gif he inne geðolian wille; ⁊ þonne ymb VII niht, gif he wille on hand gan ⁊ wæpenu sellan, gehealde hine XXX nihta gesundne ⁊ hine his mægum gebodie ⁊ his friondum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="75" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn er Macht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.de.1"/> [genug<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.de.2"/>] hat, dass er seinen Feind [mit Fehde] überziehen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.de.3"/> und in [dessen] Hofe belagern kann, so halte er ihn drinnen 7 Nächte und fechte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.de.4"/> nicht gegen ihn, vorausgesetzt, dass jener drinnen [so lange] ausdauern will; und dann nach 7 Nächten, wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.de.5"/> jener sich unterwerfen und [seine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.de.6"/>] Waffen ausliefern will<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.de.7"/>, bewahre er ihn 30 Nächte unversehrt und melde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_42-1.lnote.de.8"/> ihn den Verwandten und Freunden jenes [Verfolgten].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If he has [enough] power to ride [in feud] against his enemy and besiege him in [his] estate, let him keep him inside 7 nights and not fight against him, provided that the other is willing to hold out inside [so long]; and then after 7 nights, if the other is willing to surrender and hand over [his] weapons, let him keep him unharmed for 30 nights and announce him to the kinsmen and friends of that [pursued man].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="83" ed="#attenborough"/>If he has power enough to surround his adversary and besiege him in his house, he shall keep him therein seven days, but he shall not fight against him if he [his adversary] will consent to remain inside [his residence]. And if, after seven days, he will submit and hand over his weapons, he shall keep him unscathed for thirty days, and send formal notice of his position to his kinsmen and friends.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="416" ed="#whitelock"/>If he has sufficient power to surround his opponent and besiege him there in his house, he is to keep him seven days inside and not fight against him, if he will remain inside; and then after seven days, if he will surrender and give up his weapons, he is to keep him unharmed for 30 days, and send notice about him to his kinsmen and his friends.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="343" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If he has sufficient force [of numbers] that he may surround his enemy and besiege him inside, let him hold him seven nights therein and not attack him, if he is willing to endure it inside; and after seven nights, if he wishes to turn himself in and give up his weapons, let him hold him unharmed for thirty nights, and summon for him his kin and his friend-group.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="270"><label>cross-reference</label> <ref target="clause:Af_5">Af 5–5.3</ref> <quote>cf. the separation of Af. 42:1-2 (invulnerability of home/church in a feud, with cross-reference) from 5, 5:3 (sanctuary)</quote></note>
