        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-1.lnote.oe.17-2" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">75</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">minor. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">minor. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Bewaffnetes Gefolge gehört zur Heimsuchung</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">An armed following is an element of hamsocn</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Genetiv bei Verben des Besitzes</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Genitive with verbs of possessing</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘bereiten’ Schmid; vielmehr ‘belagern, ergreifen, fassen’; Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘prepare’ Schmid; rather ‘besiege, seize, grasp’; Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Fränkisch heisst Heimsuchung <hi rend="italic">assalitura,</hi> daher Q’s Ausdruck. — Das ‘Fechten’ ist tödlich zu denken</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In Frankish, hamsocn is called <hi rend="italic">assalitura,</hi> hence Q’s expression. — The ‘fighting’ is to be understood as deadly</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-1.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Folgende benutzt aus Q Hn 83, 1. <hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> Asyl 8; Frist 6g. 12b</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hn 83, 1 uses what follows, from Q. <hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Asyl 8; Frist 6g. 12b</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-1.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H cor., gegen ältere Kürze. — Über diese Ergebung <hi rend="italic">o.</hi> 5, 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H cor., as against the older, shorter reading. — On this surrender <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 5, 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-1.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nach dieser Woche also geniesst Befehdeter nicht den Schutz des Hausfriedens</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">After this week, therefore, the man under feud no longer enjoys the protection of the peace of the house</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-1.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘biete an’ H Q, aber auch <hi rend="italic">gecyðe</hi> 42, 4 übersetzt Q: <hi rend="italic">offeratur.</hi> Neben Sippe (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 16h) stehen ‘Freunde’ vielleicht nicht rein tautologisch, sondern meinen daneben andere als angeborene Beziehung, z. B. Vassallität oder Patenschaft. Die Mitteilung bezweckt, dass die Freunde den am Leben Bedrohten auslösen; <hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> Af 5, 3. Unterbleibt die Auslösung, so steht Tötung dem Rächer frei; Maurer <hi rend="italic">Kr. Übsch.</hi> III 42</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘offer’ H Q; but Q also translates <hi rend="italic">gecyðe</hi> 42, 4 by <hi rend="italic">offeratur.</hi> Alongside the kindred (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 16h), ‘friends’ is perhaps not purely tautological, but also denotes relationships other than those of birth, e.g. vassalage or godparenthood. The purpose of the notification is that the friends should ransom the man whose life is threatened; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> Af 5, 3. If no ransom is paid, the avenger is free to kill him; Maurer <hi rend="italic">Kr. Übsch.</hi> III 42</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_42-1.attnote.fn.17" n="17" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">82</biblScope></bibl><label>inne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">⁊ hine inne</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_42-1.attnote.fn.18" n="18" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">82</biblScope></bibl><label>hine</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">him</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_42-1.attnote.fn.19" n="19" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">82</biblScope></bibl><label>on</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ond</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_42-1.attnote.fn.20" n="20" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">82</biblScope></bibl><label>his</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">H*.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_42-1.attnote.fn.21" n="21" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">82</biblScope></bibl><label>gebodie</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">his freondum ⁊ his magum bebeode</hi>. H.</seg></note>
      </div>
